  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5); fund balance 548,532 + 595,616 - 489,998 - net transfers 36,820 = 617,330. Transfers printed only as one net line per fund; the governmental total (36,820 net out) is recorded as transfers_out. Business-type from the proprietary statement (p7) Total column, measure net position (modified cash: cash, restricted cash and CDs less customer deposits): 252,018 + 178,484 - 256,326 + 36,820 = 210,996; total expenses 256,326 printed on the Statement of Activities (p2). Proprietary cash flow statement (p8) not recorded (aligned with FY2023/FY2024). Ending governmental cash = Total assets on the governmental funds balance sheet (all cash, p4); no beginning governmental cash printed. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds balance sheet (totals equal the government-wide governmental column, p1), business-type from p1. Detail: General Fund from the departmental combining statement (p12, General and Recreation columns), which supersedes the General Fund budget schedule (p9; budget figures not mapped to departments: General government 134,600, Park 55,250, Garbage collection 72,500; total resources 248,238, charges 262,350); Street Fund (p10) and Sales Tax Fund (p11; its heading prints 'Year Ended September 30, 2021' but the figures are FY2022's) budget schedules; no business-type detail (no utility supplementary schedule; aligned with FY2023/FY2024). Other Governmental Fund (Rehab) has no schedule and is not in detail. Street Fund Intergovernmental kept as other state aid (highway allocation not printed). Read pages 1-12 of 12"
}
